Restore the max_tau coincidence-window cap

Since 0.8.0 consolidated three per-file copies of get_tau into one shared
implementation, the final clamp went missing: max_tau now seeds the four
neighboring-ISI slots and every one of them is overwritten as soon as that
neighbor exists, so a pair interior to both trains never sees the cap. The
window returned is the minimum of the interpolated half-ISIs and max_tau is
never compared against it. Under MRTS > 0 the seeded slot enters Interpolate
as an argument rather than as an outer bound, so the cap is inert at the
edges too.

Inside get_tau the parameter named max_tau carries true_max -- the recording
span, or twice the user's cap when that doubled value is smaller -- so the
bound to apply is half of it. No max_tau > 0 guard is needed: when the user
passes 0 or None the callers set true_max to the recording span, and bounding
the window at half the span is what 0.7.0 did, since it seeded m with interval
before halving.

Reported at: docs/todo/2026-08-11-file-pyspike-max-tau-issue.md (bugarach)
Verified against PySpike v0.9.0: 56 tests over 13 collecting files pass with
this applied, on both the compiled Cython and the pure-Python backend, against
50 over 12 without it. Generated with git diff, and accepted by both git apply
and patch(1) -- tools/pyspike_patch_check.sh gates both.

